E\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PublicProfile'\n                        : name equals 'EnableFirewall'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PublicProfile\\EnableFirewall\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n","false_positives":"","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack. To be effective, it must be enabled and properly configured. This setting enables the firewall when connected to a public network.","uuid":"4E8BC197-6BF9-1014-B3F6-FC8A08955886","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security must be enabled when connected to a public network.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-241991r922932","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The preferred method of configuring the firewall settings is with a policy, particularly in a domain environment.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall Properties (this link will be in the right pane) &gt;&gt; Public Profile tab &gt;&gt; State, \"Firewall state\" to \"On (recommended)\".\n\nIn addition to using policies, systems may also be configured using the firewall GUI or Netsh commands. These methods may be more appropriate for standalone systems.\n\nThe configuration settings in the GUI are the same as those specified in the policy above. Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties will be a link in the center pane after opening Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.\n\nThe following Netsh commands may also be used to configure this setting:\n\n\"Netsh advfirewall set publicprofile state on\".\nor\n\"Netsh advfirewall set allprofiles state on\".","check_content":"If the following policy-based registry value exists and is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PublicProfile\\\n\nValue Name:  EnableFirewall\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)\n\nIf the policy-based registry value does not exist, verify the following registry value. If it is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\PublicProfile\\\n\nValue Name:  EnableFirewall\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":""},{"rule_id":"SV-241992r922934","rule_title":"Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security must block unsolicited inbound connections when connected to a domain.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"4E8BCACD-6BF9-1014-9914-B26EEBB1A5AE","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack. To be effective, it must be enabled and properly configured. Unsolicited inbound connections may be malicious attempts to gain access to a system. Unsolicited inbound connections, for which there is no rule allowing the connection, will be blocked in the domain.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:13:59\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (defaultinboundaction non existent)\nResult Analysis         :            Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!DefaultInboundAction value equals variable)\nResult Analysis         :            Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\DefaultInboundAction'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!DefaultInboundAction value equals variable)\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\DefaultInboundAction\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall non existent)\nResult Analysis         :            Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\nTest                    :       true (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall value equals variable)\nTest                    :     false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall value equals variable)\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\EnableFirewall\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:tst:480102 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title       