        : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:obj:479801 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableFirewall'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:ste:479800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value equals variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile'\n                        : name equals 'EnableFirewall'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519140000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:tst:479800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall value equals variable\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:obj:479800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableFirewall'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:ste:479800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value equals variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile'\n                        : name equals 'EnableFirewall'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\EnableFirewall\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack. To be effective, it must be enabled and properly configured. The firewall log file size for a domain connection will be set to ensure enough capacity is allocated for audit data.","check_content":"If the system is not a member of a domain, the Domain Profile requirements can be marked NA.\n\nIf the system is a member of a domain and the firewall's Domain Profile is not enabled (see V-17415), this requirement is also a finding.\n\nIf the following policy-based registry value exists and is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\Logging\\\n\nValue Name:  LogFileSize\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00004000 (16384) (or greater)\n\nIf the policy-based registry value does not exist, verify the following registry value. If it is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging\\\n\nValue Name:  LogFileSize\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00004000 (16384) (or greater)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The preferred method of configuring the firewall settings is with a policy, particularly in a domain environment.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties (this link will be in the right pane) &gt;&gt; Domain Profile tab &gt;&gt; Logging (select Customize), \"Size limit (KB):\" to \"16,384\" or greater.\n\nIn addition to using policies, systems may also be configured using the firewall GUI or Netsh commands. These methods may be more appropriate for standalone systems.\n\nThe configuration settings in the GUI are the same as those specified in the policy above. Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties will be a link in the center pane after opening Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.\n\nThe following Netsh command may also be used to configure this setting:\n\n\"Netsh advfirewall set domainprofile logging maxfilesize 16384\" or greater."},{"check_content":"If the system is not a member of a domain, the Domain Profile requirements can be marked NA.\n\nIf the system is a member of a domain and the firewall's Domain Profile is not enabled (see V-17415), this requirement is also a finding.\n\nIf the following policy-based registry value exists and is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\Logging\\\n\nValue Name:  LogDroppedPackets\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)\n\nIf the policy-based registry value does not exist, verify the following registry value. If it is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging\\\n\nValue Name:  LogDroppedPackets\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The preferred method of configuring the firewall settings is with a policy, particularly in a domain environment.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall Properties (this link will be in the right pane) &gt;&gt; Domain Profile tab &gt;&gt; Logging (select Customize), \"Log dropped packets\" to \"Yes\".\n\nIn addition to using policies, systems may also be configured using the firewall GUI or Netsh commands. These methods may be more appropriate for standalone systems.\n\nThe configuration settings in the GUI are the same as those specified in the policy above. Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties will be a link in the center pane after opening Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.\n\nThe following Netsh commands may also be used to configure this setting:\n\n\"Netsh advfirewall set domainprofile logging droppedconnections enable\".\nor\n\"Netsh advfirewall set allprofiles logging droppedconnections enable\".","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"4E8BE877-6BF9-1014-AED9-CD416B7B6193","rule_id":"SV-241995r922940","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security must log dropped packets when connected to a domain.","potential_impacts":"","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Defender_Firewall_V2R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:def:4807"},"rule_id_src":"SV-241995r922940_rule","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack. To be effective, it must be enabled and properly configured. Logging of dropped packets for a domain connection will be enabled to maintain an audit trail of potential issues.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:13:59\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging!LogDroppedPackets value equals variable)\nResult Analysis         :            HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging\\LogDroppedPackets\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\Logging!LogDroppedPackets non existent)\nResult Analysis         :            Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\nTest                    :     true (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\Logging!LogDroppedPackets value equals variable)\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall non existent)\nResult Analysis         :            Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\nTest                    :       true (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall value equals variable)\nTest                    :     false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile!EnableFirewall value equals variable)\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\EnableFirewall\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:tst:480701 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging!LogDroppedPackets value equals variable\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:obj:480701 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging!LogDroppedPackets\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\DomainProfile\\Logging'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LogDroppedPackets'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.di