(registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value equals variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : for allvalue, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     value must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PrivateProfile'\n                        : name equals 'EnableFirewall'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PrivateProfile\\EnableFirewall\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack. To be effective, it must be enabled and properly configured. Logging of successful connections for a private network connection will be enabled to maintain an audit trail if issues are discovered.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.fso.windows:def:4816","href":"U_MS_Windows_Defender_Firewall_V2R3_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-242001r922952_rule","ccis":["CCI-001462"],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security must log successful connections when connected to a private network.","rule_id":"SV-242001r922952","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"4E8C1DA3-6BF9-1014-A55D-A56DD7F3B9DD","fix_text":"The preferred method of configuring the firewall settings is with a policy, particularly in a domain environment.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties (this link will be in the right pane) &gt;&gt; Private Profile tab &gt;&gt; Logging (select Customize), \"Logged successful connections\" to \"Yes\".\n\nIn addition to using policies, systems may also be configured using the firewall GUI or Netsh commands. These methods may be more appropriate for standalone systems.\n\nThe configuration settings in the GUI are the same as those specified in the policy above. Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties will be a link in the center pane after opening Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.\n\nThe following Netsh commands may also be used to configure this setting:\n\n\"Netsh advfirewall set privateprofile logging allowedconnections enable\".\nor\n\"Netsh advfirewall set allprofiles logging allowedconnections enable\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the firewall's Private Profile is not enabled (see V-17416), this requirement is also a finding.\n\nIf the following policy-based registry value exists and is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PrivateProfile\\Logging\\\n\nValue Name:  LogSuccessfulConnections\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)\n\nIf the policy-based registry value does not exist, verify the following registry value. If it is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\StandardProfile\\Logging\\\n\nValue Name:  LogSuccessfulConnections\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)","severity":"low","group_id":"V-242001","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-242001","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"4E8AAF8E-6BF9-1014-9D83-8E1CAF7A36E8","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-242001"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["V-17437","SV-54905"],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WNFWA-000019","reference_identifier":"5363"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WNFWA-000020","reference_identifier":"5363","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-242002","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":["V-17438","SV-54906"],"severity":"high","group_id":"V-242002","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-242002","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"4E8AAF8E-6BF9-1014-9D83-8E1CAF7A36E8","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the firewall's Public Profile is not enabled (see V-17417), this requirement is also a finding.\n\nIf the following policy-based registry value exists and is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PublicProfile\\\n\nValue Name:  DefaultInboundAction\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)\n\nIf the policy-based registry value does not exist, verify the following registry value. If it is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\PublicProfile\\\n\nValue Name:  DefaultInboundAction\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The preferred method of configuring the firewall settings is with a policy, particularly in a domain environment.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall Properties (this link will be in the right pane) &gt;&gt; Public Profile tab &gt;&gt; State, \"Inbound connections\" to \"Block (default)\".\n\nIn addition to using policies, systems may also be configured using the firewall GUI or Netsh commands. These methods may be more appropriate for standalone systems.\n\nThe configuration settings in the GUI are the same as those specified in the policy above. Microsoft Defender Firewall Properties will be a link in the center pane after opening Microsoft Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.\n\nThe following Netsh commands may also be used to configure this setting:\n\n\"Netsh advfirewall set publicprofile firewallpolicy blockinbound,allowoutbound\".\nor\n\"Netsh advfirewall set allprofiles firewallpolicy blockinbound,allowoutbound\".\n\nBoth inbound and outbound parameters must be specified to execute this command.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security must block unsolicited inbound connections when connected to a public network.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-242002r922954","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"4E8C2614-6BF9-1014-BEE6-C9B54F944E74","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:13:59\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\PublicProfile!DefaultInboundAction value equals variable)\nResult Analysis         :            Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\nTest                    :       false (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\SharedAccess\\Parameters\\FirewallPolicy\\PublicProfile!DefaultInboundAction value equals variable)\nResult A